        "FRIEND: You're getting ready to gaze towards the Morea again and fall silent again… Though I have a way of making you talk whenever I like.\n\n"
        "POET: I understand: you want us to talk about the language. Do I have anything else on my mind but freedom and language? The one has begun to trample Turkish heads; the other wants soon to trample pedants' heads; and then, arm in arm, the two will go forward on the road of glory, never turning back if some pedant caws or some Turk barks: for to me the two are alike.\n\n"
